Bootstrap: docker
From: node:20-bookworm-slim

# ── How this image serves the web ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SPA is built ONLINE (on a host that can reach npm) BEFORE `apptainer build`, and the built
# `apps/web/dist` is BAKED into the image (%files below). The container then serves that static dist
# with a tiny baked-in static server (`serve`) — it does NOT run pnpm/corepack at start, so it works
# on cae00's TLS-intercept network where npm is unreachable.
#
# The /api proxy that vite-dev/preview used to provide is handled by the FRONT layer instead: behind
# the HWAX portal, nginx forwards /mx-white-paper/api → the API. (Standalone, point your own proxy or
# set VITE_API_URL to the API origin.)
#
# CRITICAL: the dist is base-path-specific. Build it ONLINE with the SAME prefix cae00 serves under:
#   MXWP_BASE_PATH=/mx-white-paper/ pnpm --filter @mx/web build   (then `apptainer build web.sif`)

%labels
    Maintainer  squall321@gmail.com
    Component   mxwp-web
    Version     0.2.0

%files
    # Prebuilt SPA (must exist on the ONLINE builder before `apptainer build`).
    apps/web/dist /opt/web/dist

%post
    set -eux
    # Bake a tiny static file server while we're still online; no runtime npm needed.
    npm install -g serve@14
    # Keep pnpm for the interactive %runscript dev path (online machines only).
    corepack disable 2>/dev/null || true
    npm install -g pnpm@9.12.0
    mkdir -p /workspace /opt/web/dist

%environment
    export PATH=/usr/local/bin:$PATH
    export PNPM_HOME=/root/.local/share/pnpm
    export PATH=$PNPM_HOME:$PATH

%runscript
    # Interactive DEV (HMR) — ONLINE machines only (needs pnpm/network). Not used on cae00.
    cd /workspace
    pnpm install --frozen-lockfile=false
    pnpm schema:gen
    exec pnpm --filter @mx/web dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173 "$@"

%startscript
    # PRODUCTION: serve the BAKED, prebuilt dist statically. No pnpm, no build, no network.
    # `serve -s` does SPA fallback (any unknown path → index.html). The dist already has the base
    # path baked into its asset/router URLs, so the front nginx serves it under that prefix
    # (the HWAX portal strips /mx-white-paper/ and forwards to this serve at the root).
    # Detach with setsid+nohup so the daemon survives the startscript shell returning (an `exec`
    # here gets reaped — the instance then has NO running process and :5173 never opens).
    setsid nohup serve -s /opt/web/dist -l tcp://0.0.0.0:5173 > /tmp/serve.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &

%help
    MX White Paper Web container (static-serve of a prebuilt SPA).
    PRODUCTION (cae00, no build): online → `MXWP_BASE_PATH=/mx-white-paper/ pnpm --filter @mx/web build`
      → `apptainer build web.sif web.def` (bakes apps/web/dist) → push via images-to-drive.sh →
      cae00 `images-from-drive.sh` + `start.sh` → instance runs `serve -s /opt/web/dist`.
    DEV (online): `apptainer run web.sif` → vite dev with HMR.
    /api is proxied by the front layer (HWAX portal nginx: /mx-white-paper/api → API), not here.
